    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Wicomico Parish Church was established by the Virginia Assembly between 1645 and 1647, making it one of the Commonwealth's oldest parishes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wicomicoepiscopal.org/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first church was a modest wooden structure built in the 1650s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wicomicoepiscopal.org/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A brick building erected around 1686 marked the parish's growing permanence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wicomicoepiscopal.org/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1771, a third church was completed, then the largest colonial church in Virginia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wicomicoepiscopal.org/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The present church, on the original site, was finished in 1902, with a Parish House added in 1954.",
